Remove text from one agent file that repeats rules the same file already states elsewhere, and
bring its advisor block to the shared wording where the changes below say so. Every change is a
deletion, a section renumbering that follows a deletion, or a re-wrap of the advisor block. No
rule is reworded.

The two files are the canonical file and its twin. Each has its own list of changes below,
because the twin's text can differ in path strings. Apply each list to its own file.

Files:
1. .skilled/agents/code.md
2. .claude/agents/code.md

Do not touch the frontmatter. A commit hook raises the `version` field.
Each change below gives the exact text to find (OLD) and the exact text that replaces it (NEW).
The first and last lines of OLD and NEW are unchanged context lines, shown so the place is unambiguous.
Blank lines inside OLD and NEW are part of the text. Apply every change, top to bottom.

